}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3-12 rows x 3-12 cols
  colors:
    background: any single color (most common, 55-70% of cells)
    foreground: one other color (30-45% of cells)
  foreground_paths:
    count: 1-4 non-branching 4-connected paths
    structure: each cell has degree 1 or 2 (simple chain, no branches)
    endpoints: both endpoints of each path lie on a grid border
    border_touches: each path connects two (possibly same) borders
    cells_per_row_in_component: 1-3 typical, max 5
    turns_per_path: 1-11 (more turns for longer paths)
    path_length: 4-23 cells
  background_regions:
    count: 2-5 (4-connected), equals number_of_fg_paths + 1
    min_region_size: >=1 cell
  output:
    shape: (num_bg_regions, 1) single-column grid
    fill: all cells are background color

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (paths partition background into target region count)
  steps:
    1. Choose grid dimensions H x W (3-12 each), bg color, fg color, target N bg regions (2-5).
    2. Need N-1 non-branching paths to partition the grid into N regions.
    3. For each path, pick two border cells as endpoints; grow a random-walk 4-connected chain between them (no branching, no self-intersection, no touching other paths except at border-adjacent cells). Ensure the path separates at least one new bg region.
    4. Verify that bg has exactly N 4-connected regions. Retry path placement if not.
    5. Output is an Nx1 grid filled with bg color.
```
